# Content script and page-world

## Boundaries

- Content script and page-world are vanilla TypeScript — never mount React on x.com.
- Keep the Nostr secret key and signing imports out of these packages.
- Isolate injected UI with Shadow DOM; styles stay inside the shadow root.
- Never modify X's existing requests or responses; GraphQL proof search is a separate extension-initiated fetch.

## DOM and SPA

- Prefer semantic post attributes and Schema.org metadata over generated classes; `data-testid` is a compatibility fallback only.
- Discover author name rows, chips, and badges through `scanner.ts` helpers (`findAuthorNameRow`, chip slots, verified badge) so ambient/chip mounts survive X markup churn. Keep lookups article-scoped for speed.
- Make mounts idempotent and compatible with SPA navigation and dynamically inserted posts.
- Preserve X's existing behavior; do not intercept clicks or rewrite host UI outside the panel/chip hosts.

## Page-world → content bridge

- Passive observer: clone allowlisted successful JSON only; discard raw payloads after extracting public tuples.
- Forward only validated, normalized records (`twitterId`, handle, post IDs, etc.) — never raw GraphQL bodies, cookies, or bearer tokens.
- Proof-search GraphQL may run only under the triggers in `x-identity.mdc`; forward validated proof matches only.

## Trust UI hot path

- Batch visible account/post IDs via `QUERY_TRUST_BATCH` (roughly 20–50), not one RPC per cell.
- Debounce/coalesce with the existing scan timer (~180 ms).
- Do not read IndexedDB from the content script for trust answers — query the service worker.

## Build

- Content and page bundles are self-contained IIFEs (`vite.content.config.ts`, `vite.page.config.ts`).
- Content-script strings use `src/i18n/resources.ts` (`en`/`da`); see `internationalization.mdc`.
